# E15 Fictitious Play: parallel; the game agent and the two players print in the same turns, in any order between them,
# and a message sent during a turn may be read in that turn or the next: where a player's line falls between the round
# lines of the game agent depends on the interleaving. Compared: the lines of the game agent in order (round lines
# included), the lines of each player in order, and all the messages as a multiset.
ignore ^$
cover all
fact game ^(Starting fictitious play .*|--- Round \d+ ---|Joint action: .*|Game finished\.|Total payoff for .*)$
fact play ^(player\d) \(round (\d+)\) plays ([CD])$
fact observe ^(player\d) observes opponent played ([CD]), payoff = (.*)$
fact player ^(player\d)(: stopping\.|: belief about .*|: empirical strategy: .*)$
fact message ^\t\[(\w+) -> (\w+)\]: (.*)$
same game seq
same play seq by 0
same observe seq by 0
same player seq by 0
same message bag
check play count == 100
check observe count == 100
